This has a real spine. The core idea is strong: **self-mastery treated as open-source human systems engineering**. I tightened the language and transitions without sanding off your voice.

## Why am I posting this on GitHub like it is a piece of software?

Because perhaps, in a way, it is.

Growing up, I was always told that the key to success was self-mastery, usually followed by some hand-wavy bullshit.

Well, I have a little living behind me now, along with plenty of baggage I am still working through, like everyone else.

I thought perhaps I could share what I learn through personal introspection while helping myself build a map of the terrain.

Self-mastery and self-improvement have been commodified and sold to the public in a way that poisons the process. A holistic human practice gets fragmented into marketable domains, stripped of context, and sold back to us in pieces.

Stay with me, fam. Let us take a crack at this engineering problem.

I will attempt to share my thoughts in a secular way. Fair warning, I am Catholic officially, Gnostic and mystical by inclination, and incurably curious. I am not someone who fits cleanly into a box. I am a human being on a spiritual journey, and I hope not to offend anyone along the way.

Please feel free to iterate, improve, modify, and adapt these exercises.

This is not meant to be a bible, at least not yet. It is a primer. I intend to constrain the scope and present the foundational practices clearly enough that someone can begin with the fundamentals and discover the rest for themselves.

Religion and spiritual practice often become entangled with the collective ego of their communities. I suppose that is ordinary human behavior.

My goal is to focus on the foundations that allow the human organism to adapt and succeed under changing conditions, and through that work contribute to a stronger and more resilient civilization.

Civilizations are made of individuals. Individuals belong to families and every larger social body built from them. These societies are shaped by culture, and culture is carried through customs.

**Customs are a technology that shapes human behavior at scale.**

The Self-Mastery Primer is therefore an attempt to cultivate customs, habits, and mental models that optimize for agency and self-knowledge.

Modern culture has adopted an increasingly materialistic view of the human being. That view often misses the layered nature of the human organism and therefore fails to address the upstream causes of destructive behavior in ourselves and others.

